[{:db/id 17592186204239 :question/problem "Let $A=R,$ and consider the relation \"greater than or equal to\" on $A.$ Express the relation using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\nR=\\{{{field-1}}\\in {{field-2}}\\,:\\,{{field-3}}\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nFor a relation $R$ on a set $A,$ we also have the following notations:\n\n- $a\\,R\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\in R$\n\n- $a\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}$ such that $x\\ge y.$\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge y\\}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186411680 :question/problem "Let $A=Z,$ and consider the relation $R$ on $A$ such that $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $3\\,|\\,(x+y).$ Express $R$ using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\nR=\\{{{field-1}}\\in {{field-2}}\\,:\\,{{field-3}}\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nFor a relation $R$ on a set $A,$ we also have the following notations:\n\n- $a\\,R\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\in R$\n\n- $a\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}$ such that $3\\,|\\,(x+y).$\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,3\\,|\\,(x+y)\\}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
